{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetD72UToMhLLoTQvrXtj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the context I need. Now let me present my analysis summary:\n\n**Repository findings** (current code locations):\n- Shipment model: `Shipment.kt:9-14` — defines shipmentId, orderId, carrier, status\n- ShipmentStatus enum: `Shipment.kt:23-27` — CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController: `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — currently has create, getById, list (no confirm endpoint)\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository: `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — save, findById, existsById, findAll methods\n- Exception handling: `ApiExceptions.kt:11-31` — ResourceNotFoundException (404), ConflictException (409)\n- Error codes: `ApiError.kt:31-37` — SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS, etc. (no SHIPMENT_CANCELLED code yet)\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-29` — converts ApiException to ApiError response\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers directly use repository; throw ConflictException for 409, ResourceNotFoundException for 404\n2. State-changing endpoints return `ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.CREATED).body(object)` or similar\n3. Error responses follow the envelope structure: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`\n4. Tests use MockMvc with `status()` and `jsonPath()` assertions, clearing repository in `@BeforeEach`\n5. Tests verify error codes with `jsonPath(\"$.error.code\")`, not just status codes\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` — must add SHIPMENT_CANCELLED error code (needed for 409 response)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add confirm endpoint method\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for confirm behavior\n\n**Risks:**\n1. If the SHIPMENT_CANCELLED code is not added, cannot return proper 409 with consistent error envelope\n2. Idempotency requirement means confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment must succeed and return the unchanged shipment\n3. Tests must verify state persists through repository, not just response body (per testing-and-verification skill)\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone — the ticket clearly specifies all state transitions and error responses.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to the ErrorCode enum (line 36, before the closing brace). This provides the error code for rejecting confirm on a cancelled shipment.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new endpoint method:\n   - Route: `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`\n   - Logic:\n     - Fetch shipment by ID; if not found, throw ResourceNotFoundException (existing pattern)\n     - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED code (409)\n     - If status is CREATED, update status to CONFIRMED and save\n     - If status is CONFIRMED, do nothing (idempotent)\n     - Return the shipment (whether changed or not)\n   - Return ResponseEntity.ok().body(shipment) for success (200 OK, shipment in body)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirmCreatedShipment()` — POST confirm on CREATED shipment, verify 200 response, verify response body shows CONFIRMED, then GET the shipment and verify it persists as CONFIRMED\n   - `confirmAlreadyConfirmedShipment()` — POST confirm on already-CONFIRMED shipment, verify 200 response, verify response body is CONFIRMED (idempotent), then GET and verify unchanged\n   - `confirmCancelledShipmentReturnsConflict()` — Set up shipment in CANCELLED state (via repository), POST confirm, expect 409, verify error.code is SHIPMENT_CANCELLED, then GET and verify shipment is still CANCELLED\n   - `confirmNonExistentShipmentReturnsNotFound()` — POST confirm on non-existent shipment ID, expect 404, verify error.code is SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, then GET and verify still missing\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\nI considered creating a ShipmentService layer between controller and repository to handle status transitions, but the existing codebase has no service layer (OrderController calls repository directly), so adding one would violate the \"preserve existing architecture\" constraint and add unrelated refactoring.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Logic | Write | Response | Via |\n|------|------|-------|-------|----------|-----|\n| CREATED→CONFIRMED | repo.findById(id) | Check status, update to CONFIRMED | repo.save(updated) | 200 OK + shipment JSON | ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| Repeat CONFIRMED | repo.findById(id) | Check status=CONFIRMED, no-op | (none) | 200 OK + same shipment JSON | ResponseEntity.ok(shipment) |\n| CANCELLED reject | repo.findById(id) | Check status=CANCELLED | (none) | 409 Conflict + error envelope | throw ConflictException |\n| Not found | repo.findById(id)=null | Not found | (none) | 404 Not Found + error envelope | throw ResourceNotFoundException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n- **confirmCreatedShipment()** — covers the happy path (CREATED→CONFIRMED transition) and verifies persistence\n- **confirmAlreadyConfirmedShipment()** — covers idempotency requirement; asserts the response body and verifies via second GET that nothing changed\n- **confirmCancelledShipmentReturnsConflict()** — covers the CANCELLED rejection case, asserts error.code, and verifies the state is not mutated by the rejected call\n- **confirmNonExistentShipmentReturnsNotFound()** — covers the 404 case, asserts error.code, and verifies no side effects\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll write the code. Let me start by adding the error code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":237,"cache_read_input_tokens":20396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":237},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":nul